<title>EGYPT: Egypt cotton exports detailed.</title>
<headline>Egypt cotton exports detailed.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt exported 321 tonnes of cotton in the past two weeks, the Alexandria Cotton Exporters Association (Alcotexa) said on Monday.</p>
<p>The cumulative total for cotton export commitments this season, now in the 23rd week, rises to 62,668 tonnes, said Alcotexa, which coordinates prices and exports by private and state-owned firms.</p>
<p>Of the 321 tonnes, German companies bought 201 tonnes, Turkey 99 tonnes and South Korea 21.</p>
<p>Egypt has said it expects to export between 125,000 and 150,000 tonnes from last year's harvest.</p>
<p>-- Esmat Salaheddin +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
